{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-06-12T18:55:54.817Z","tool_name":"invoke_agent","tool_id":"invoke_agent__qi9rtlox","parameters":{"agent_name":"generalist","prompt":"You are an expert Rust engineering subagent working on the `underrated` web browser engine. Your task is to complete the migration of layout and paint consumers to the new `CategorizedComputedStyle` struct.\n\n### Completed So Far\n- `src/style/categorized.rs` has all the fields, setters, getters, and set_property.\n- `src/style/mod.rs` is rewritten to produce `HashMap<NodeId, CategorizedComputedStyle>`.\n- `src/engine/mod.rs`, `src/engine/flush.rs`, and `src/script/mod.rs` are completely migrated.\n\n### Remaining Files to Migrate\n1. `src/paint/stacking.rs`\n2. `src/paint/mod.rs`\n3. `src/layout/float.rs`\n4. `src/layout/position.rs`\n5. `src/layout/flex.rs`\n6. `src/layout/inline.rs`\n7. `src/layout/table.rs`\n8. `src/layout/mod.rs`\n\n### Detailed Migration Guidelines\n- Change `ComputedStyle` to `CategorizedComputedStyle` in all remaining layout and paint files.\n- Replace all `.get(\"...\")` style reads with direct typed field accesses per the cheat sheet.\n- For lengths and numeric fields represented as `i32` or `u32` (like `width`, `height`, margins, borders, font_size, line_height), they are already parsed and stored as pixels in the typed fields! Therefore, you can replace the old `if let Some(CssValue::Length(v, _)) = style.get(...)` logic with direct access to the `i32`/`u32` value (converted to `f32` as needed). No unit parsing or matching of `CssValue` variants is required anymore!\n- To check if auto-able properties (like `width`, `height`, margins, top/right/bottom/left, flex-basis) are `auto`/unspecified, check if they are equal to `-1`.\n- For `vertical-align` (`vertical_align: i32` field in `ResetBox`):\n  - `-1` -> `\"baseline\"`\n  - `-2` -> `\"sub\"`\n  - `-3` -> `\"super\"`\n  - `-4` -> `\"top\"` or `\"text-top\"`\n  - `-5` -> `\"bottom\"` or `\"text-bottom\"`\n  - `-6` -> `\"middle\"`\n  - Otherwise, if the value is `>= 50000`, the actual raise length in pixels is `(value - 100000) as f32`. Else it is `value as f32`.\n- For `z-index` (`z_index: i32` field in `ResetBox`):\n  - `i32::MIN` -> `\"auto\"` or `ZIndex::Auto`.\n  - Otherwise, `ZIndex::Index(z_index)`.\n- Replace any test writes from `style.insert(...)` to the corresponding COW setters (e.g. `.set_width(i32)`, `.set_height(i32)`, `.set_z_index(i32)`) or `.set_property(\"...\", &value)`.\n- Keep running `cargo check` and fixing compiler errors sequentially. Be extremely focused, precise, and fast so you complete within your turn budget.\n","wait_for_previous":true}}
